hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"375","Na Muhammad bin Rafi’, Na Abd al-Razzaq, Ma’mar told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qilaba, on the authority of Anas, he said: “Bilal used to praise The call to prayer and the Iqamah are made in Witr prayers, except for his saying: “The prayer has begun,” “The prayer has begun.” Abu Bakr said: Ibn al-Muthanna reported on the authority of Ibn Umar on this topic."
"376","On the authority of Muhammad ibn Muammar al-Qaysi, on the authority of Sulayman ibn Harb, on the authority of Hammad ibn Zayd, on the authority of Samak ibn Atiya, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qilabah, on the authority of Anas said: “Bilal was commanded to recite the call to prayer, and to pronounce the Iqamat Witr, except for the Iqamat, meaning the prayer has begun.”"
